13	 * consumed both by the response mapper and by the create pipeline's identity check, so it lives in the
14	 * model layer rather than beside the pipeline functions.
15	 *
16	 * <p>It deliberately folds the former separate telephone, email and household duplicate checks into
17	 * one comparison. Because the telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and
18	 * postcode but different telephones have different keys and are both allowed (they are instead flagged
19	 * as a soft match) — only an exact full-key match is a hard duplicate.
20	 *
21	 * <p>The components are normalized the same way for a submitted owner and a stored one, so values with
22	 * incidental telephone formatting or email casing still match: the telephone is run through
23	 * {@link OwnerTelephone#toE164(String)}, the email is lower-cased, and the last name is reduced to its
24	 * {@link Soundex} code. A {@code null} component contributes the empty string.
25	 */
